{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40709","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66193","text":"Slice B, Commit 4 — the runtime fold: closure memo "},{"id":"spn-66194","marks":["bold"],"text":"and one blocking question"}]},{"id":"blk-40710","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66195","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-66196","text":" the commit is CLOSED at the golden layer and "},{"id":"spn-66197","marks":["bold"],"text":"cannot close natively without a ruling."},{"id":"spn-66198","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66199","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run49"},{"id":"spn-66200","text":" PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (28s, 67 rows). "},{"id":"spn-66201","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate49"},{"id":"spn-66202","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66203","marks":["bold"],"text":"22/22 ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"spn-66204","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-66205","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep"},{"id":"spn-66206","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66207","marks":["bold"],"text":"18/18 green"},{"id":"spn-66208","text":" (184s, reference + native), L-0 tier unmoved."}]},{"id":"blk-40711","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66209","text":"Commits 2 and 3 gave a route a canonical form, an identity, a locator and a ruled spelling, and both closure memos ended with the same admission: a route is carried, sealed, formatted, refused for every reason it should be — "},{"id":"spn-66210","marks":["bold"],"text":"and provably ignored at runtime."},{"id":"spn-66211","text":" That stops being true here. A "},{"id":"spn-66212","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66213","text":" written in text now fires:"}]},{"id":"blk-40712","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"ep1  ledger:MailboxEnqueue,mailbox=mb,epoch=1  next_inbox=(w15.s0.4e.2.0.0.0.0.7->mb[0.0.0.7])\nep2  ledger:MailboxDeliver,mailbox=mb,epoch=2  inbox=(w15.s0.4e...)\nep3  inbox=(),next_inbox=()\nreceipt:w=15,s=0,accepted=4e,apkey=2.0.0.0.0.7,epoch=1,outcome=Applied"},{"id":"blk-40713","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66214","marks":["bold"],"text":"§2 is the only part that blocks."},{"id":"spn-66215","text":" Everything else is a decision to confirm or overrule at leisure."}]},{"id":"blk-40714","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66216","text":"0. Running the packet"}]},{"id":"blk-40715","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66217","text":"Every number in this memo is reproducible from the zip alone, with nothing but a Python 3 and (optionally) a C compiler:"}]},{"id":"blk-40716","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"unzip WRL_SLICE_B_COMMIT4_PACKET.zip && cd forge\npython3 run_l0_sweep.py                   # 18/18 green -- RUN THIS FIRST\npython3 binding_run49.py                  # the commit under review, 67 rows\nTRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 mutate49.py    # 22/22 ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"blk-40717","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66218","marks":["bold"],"text":"`run_l0_sweep.py` first is not a style preference."},{"id":"spn-66219","text":" It is the only entry point that builds "},{"id":"spn-66220","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-66221","text":" from the shipped "},{"id":"spn-66222","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/c/ic32.c"},{"id":"spn-66223","text":"; the individual batteries resolve a "},{"id":"spn-66224","marks":["bold"],"text":"prebuilt"},{"id":"spn-66225","text":" binary and predate the override. Run "},{"id":"spn-66226","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run49.py"},{"id":"spn-66227","text":" standalone on a fresh extraction and it dies on R13 with a raw "},{"id":"spn-66228","marks":["code"],"text":"FileNotFoundError"},{"id":"spn-66229","text":" — measured, not guessed. Either run the sweep first, or use "},{"id":"spn-66230","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1 python3 binding_run49.py"},{"id":"spn-66231","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-66232","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_ONLY"},{"id":"spn-66233","text":", 26s), which exercises every law in the battery; native adds an independent second reducer, not new laws."}]},{"id":"blk-40718","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66234","text":"Verified from a clean extraction into an empty directory before shipping: "},{"id":"spn-66235","marks":["code"],"text":"ALL PASS -- 18/18 green (184s)"},{"id":"spn-66236","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-66237","marks":["code"],"text":"built ic32 into runtime/c/ic32 with gcc"},{"id":"spn-66238","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66239","marks":["code"],"text":"MUTATION VERDICT: ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"spn-66240","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-66241","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run49"},{"id":"spn-66242","text":" at both "},{"id":"spn-66243","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-66244","text":" (28s, 67 rows, after the sweep) and "},{"id":"spn-66245","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_ONLY"},{"id":"spn-66246","text":" (26s, standalone). Run standalone on a fresh extraction "},{"id":"spn-66247","marks":["italic"],"text":"without"},{"id":"spn-66248","text":" the sweep it fails exactly as described above — "},{"id":"spn-66249","marks":["code"],"text":"R13 raised FileNotFoundError … runtime/c/ic32"},{"id":"spn-66250","text":" — which is also measured, not asserted."}]},{"id":"blk-40719","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66251","text":"The file list is "},{"id":"spn-66252","marks":["bold"],"text":"computed"},{"id":"spn-66253","text":", not hand-written — "},{"id":"spn-66254","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/tools/build_packet.py"},{"id":"spn-66255","text":" walks the closure and "},{"id":"spn-66256","marks":["code"],"text":"--verify"},{"id":"spn-66257","text":" extracts the finished zip into an empty temp directory and runs the sweep there. Three separate walks are needed, and the packet is only correct because the third was forced by a failure rather than foreseen:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40721","spans":[{"id":"spn-66258","text":"Walk"}]},{"id":"blk-40722","spans":[{"id":"spn-66259","text":"Finds"}]},{"id":"blk-40723","spans":[{"id":"spn-66260","text":"Why an import walk alone is not enough"}]}],"id":"blk-40720","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40724","spans":[{"id":"spn-66261","text":"imports ("},{"id":"spn-66262","marks":["code"],"text":"ast"},{"id":"spn-66263","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-40725","spans":[{"id":"spn-66264","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_fold"},{"id":"spn-66265","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66266","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-66267","text":", …"}]},{"id":"blk-40726","spans":[{"id":"spn-66268","text":"—"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40727","spans":[{"id":"spn-66269","text":"subprocess targets"}]},{"id":"blk-40728","spans":[{"id":"spn-66270","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run5…50"}]},{"id":"blk-40729","spans":[{"id":"spn-66271","text":"the sweep registers batteries as bare "},{"id":"spn-66272","marks":["bold"],"text":"strings"},{"id":"spn-66273","text":" and shells out; an import walk ships the sweep without the batteries it sweeps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40730","spans":[{"id":"spn-66274","text":"data assets"}]},{"id":"blk-40731","spans":[{"id":"spn-66275","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_v1_term_fingerprints.txt"}]},{"id":"blk-40732","spans":[{"id":"spn-66276","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run50"},{"id":"spn-66277","text":" opens it by name beside itself — neither an import nor a subprocess target"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40733","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66278","text":"The first build of this packet passed its own closure check and then failed "},{"id":"spn-66279","marks":["code"],"text":"--verify"},{"id":"spn-66280","text":" at "},{"id":"spn-66281","marks":["bold"],"text":"17/18"},{"id":"spn-66282","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66283","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run50"},{"id":"spn-66284","text":" dying on "},{"id":"spn-66285","marks":["code"],"text":"FileNotFoundError"},{"id":"spn-66286","text":". It passes in-tree for the uninteresting reason that the file is simply there. That is the whole argument for extraction-verifying a packet instead of reasoning about its manifest: the previous round shipped the batteries and omitted "},{"id":"spn-66287","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/python/ic_ref.py"},{"id":"spn-66288","text":", so every battery died at import, and the round before "},{"id":"spn-66289","marks":["italic"],"text":"described"},{"id":"spn-66290","text":" a packet that was never built at all. A packet whose contents cannot be run is a claim, not evidence."}]},{"id":"blk-40734","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66291","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40736","spans":[{"id":"spn-66292","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-40737","spans":[{"id":"spn-66293","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-40735","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40738","spans":[{"id":"spn-66294","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_fold.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40739","spans":[{"id":"spn-66295","marks":["bold"],"text":"NEW."},{"id":"spn-66296","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66297","marks":["code"],"text":"route_claims"},{"id":"spn-66298","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66299","marks":["code"],"text":"route_claims_by_epoch"},{"id":"spn-66300","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66301","marks":["code"],"text":"fold_batches"},{"id":"spn-66302","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66303","marks":["code"],"text":"fold_script"},{"id":"spn-66304","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66305","marks":["code"],"text":"epoch_batch_census"},{"id":"spn-66306","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66307","marks":["code"],"text":"check_epoch_batch_capacity"},{"id":"spn-66308","text":"; plus the "},{"id":"spn-66309","marks":["bold"],"text":"declared-policy seam"},{"id":"spn-66310","text":" (§3d) — "},{"id":"spn-66311","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_policy_of"},{"id":"spn-66312","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66313","marks":["code"],"text":"film_schema_of"},{"id":"spn-66314","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66315","marks":["code"],"text":"film_mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-66316","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66317","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime_seams"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40740","spans":[{"id":"spn-66318","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_canonical.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40741","spans":[{"id":"spn-66319","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_ROUTE_BATCH_OVERFLOW"},{"id":"spn-66320","text":" (seal-time co-firing bound), "},{"id":"spn-66321","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_EPOCH_BATCH_OVERFLOW"},{"id":"spn-66322","text":" (fold-time pairing bound)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40742","spans":[{"id":"spn-66323","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40743","spans":[{"id":"spn-66324","marks":["code"],"text":"check_epoch_batch_capacity"},{"id":"spn-66325","text":" composed into "},{"id":"spn-66326","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40744","spans":[{"id":"spn-66327","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40745","spans":[{"id":"spn-66328","text":"the commit-2/3 route refusal in "},{"id":"spn-66329","marks":["code"],"text":"ir_to_fixture"},{"id":"spn-66330","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66331","marks":["bold"],"text":"lifted"},{"id":"spn-66332","text":" (§3b)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40746","spans":[{"id":"spn-66333","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run3o.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40747","spans":[{"id":"spn-66334","text":"eight helpers given a defaulted "},{"id":"spn-66335","marks":["code"],"text":"fx=None"},{"id":"spn-66336","text":" (§3f) — additive, frozen rows byte-identical"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40748","spans":[{"id":"spn-66337","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40749","spans":[{"id":"spn-66338","text":"P8d/P8e "},{"id":"spn-66339","marks":["bold"],"text":"reversed"},{"id":"spn-66340","text":" to measure the lift; "},{"id":"spn-66341","marks":["code"],"text":"_fold"},{"id":"spn-66342","text":" latent defect closed (§3f)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40750","spans":[{"id":"spn-66343","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run49.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40751","spans":[{"id":"spn-66344","marks":["bold"],"text":"NEW"},{"id":"spn-66345","text":", R1–R13"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40752","spans":[{"id":"spn-66346","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate49.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40753","spans":[{"id":"spn-66347","marks":["bold"],"text":"NEW"},{"id":"spn-66348","text":", 22 mutations"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40754","spans":[{"id":"spn-66349","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep.py"}]},{"id":"blk-40755","spans":[{"id":"spn-66350","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run49"},{"id":"spn-66351","text":" registered in the LIVE tier"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66352","text":"The whole runtime image of a route is "},{"id":"spn-66353","marks":["bold"],"text":"one ADMIT claim envelope"},{"id":"spn-66354","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-40757","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"mk_claim(ROUTE_WRITER_ID, canonical_route_ordinal, (\"Send\", mailbox_id, body))"},{"id":"blk-40758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66355","text":"No new runtime construct, no new identity rung, no widened reducer. "},{"id":"spn-66356","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"},{"id":"spn-66357","text":" is D9's tag 2, which Slice A froze; commit 4 is merely the first thing that constructs one from a language surface."}]},{"id":"blk-40759","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66358","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-66359","marks":["bold"],"text":"THE BLOCKING QUESTION"},{"id":"spn-66360","text":" — the reduced proof profile has no "},{"id":"spn-66361","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"}]},{"id":"blk-40760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66362","text":"R12 is not in the ruling and is not a request for a feature. It is a measurement, and it is the reason this battery says "},{"id":"spn-66363","marks":["italic"],"text":"golden layer only"},{"id":"spn-66364","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40761","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"WKIND=1  WIDX=3  WLANE=8  WD=8  WK=4     CKEY_W=44   FKEY_W=52   EKEY_W=8\n('Send','mb',(0,0,0,7))  payload_key -> (2,0,0,0,0,7)\n                         pack_ckey   -> AssertionError: field 2 overflows width 1\nadmit_ic.py  occurrences of \"mailbox\" or \"Send\" : 0\nruntime/c/ic32.c            occurrences of \"mailbox\" : 0"},{"id":"blk-40762","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66365","marks":["code"],"text":"WKIND"},{"id":"spn-66366","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-66367","marks":["bold"],"text":"one bit"},{"id":"spn-66368","text":", sized for "},{"id":"spn-66369","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor=0 | ResetFault=1"},{"id":"spn-66370","text":". "},{"id":"spn-66371","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"},{"id":"spn-66372","text":" is 2. A route's claim cannot be packed into the reduced profile at all, so it cannot reach "},{"id":"spn-66373","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-66374","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66375","text":"Three things make this precise rather than an excuse:"}]},{"id":"blk-40764","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40766","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66376","marks":["bold"],"text":"The boundary is exactly half."},{"id":"spn-66377","text":" R12d/R12e measure it: the route-bearing"}]}],"id":"blk-40765","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66378","text":"world's "},{"id":"spn-66379","marks":["bold"],"text":"world half"},{"id":"spn-66380","text":" crosses intact — same fixture, same initial-state keys as the route-free twin, "},{"id":"spn-66381","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == golden"},{"id":"spn-66382","text":". A mailbox costs the world state nothing; it lives in "},{"id":"spn-66383","marks":["bold"],"text":"claim"},{"id":"spn-66384","text":" state. Only the claim half is missing."}]},{"id":"blk-40768","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40770","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66385","marks":["bold"],"text":"The gap is Slice A's, not Slice B's."},{"id":"spn-66386","text":" Slice A shipped "},{"id":"spn-66387","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"},{"id":"spn-66388","text":" into the"}]}],"id":"blk-40769","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66389","text":"golden reducer, into "},{"id":"spn-66390","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanV1"},{"id":"spn-66391","text":" and into Film v0.7 without ever lowering it to IC. Commit 4 is the first caller to try to fold one."}]},{"id":"blk-40772","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40774","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66392","marks":["bold"],"text":"R13/R13b keep the native closure honest"},{"id":"spn-66393","text":" for every world that has no"}]}],"id":"blk-40773","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66394","text":"route — the frozen demo still folds "},{"id":"spn-66395","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32 == golden"},{"id":"spn-66396","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40776","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66397","text":"The gap is exactly ONE BIT — measured, not estimated"}]},{"id":"blk-40777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66398","marks":["code"],"text":"WKIND"},{"id":"spn-66399","text":" must hold 3 values ("},{"id":"spn-66400","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor=0 | ResetFault=1 | Send=2"},{"id":"spn-66401","text":"), so it needs "},{"id":"spn-66402","marks":["bold"],"text":"2"},{"id":"spn-66403","text":" bits, not 1. Everything else in "},{"id":"spn-66404","marks":["code"],"text":"CKEY_W"},{"id":"spn-66405","text":" is already at its minimum:"}]},{"id":"blk-40778","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"minimum CKEY_W for a full-budget route world:\n   WD 8  +  WKIND 2  +  WIDX 3  +  4*WLANE 32   =  45\n   today's CKEY_W                               =  44     short by ONE bit\n   implied FKEY_W = 2*WK + CKEY_W               =  53     (today 52)"},{"id":"blk-40779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66406","text":"So the whole ruling reduces to: "},{"id":"spn-66407","marks":["bold"],"text":"where does one bit come from?"},{"id":"spn-66408","text":" There are only four places, and each is now measured rather than guessed."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40781","spans":[{"id":"spn-66409","text":"source"}]},{"id":"blk-40782","spans":[{"id":"spn-66410","text":"keeps "},{"id":"spn-66411","marks":["code"],"text":"CKEY_W=44"},{"id":"spn-66412","text":"?"}]},{"id":"blk-40783","spans":[{"id":"spn-66413","text":"measured cost"}]}],"id":