ResetFault -> orb_index      max index = 0\nkind 2  Send -> mailbox_index        max index = 0"},{"id":"blk-40817","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66498","text":"Nothing shipped today needs more than index 1. That is an argument for "},{"id":"spn-66499","marks":["code"],"text":"WIDX=2"},{"id":"spn-66500","text":" being "},{"id":"spn-66501","marks":["italic"],"text":"survivable in practice"},{"id":"spn-66502","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66503","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-66504","text":" an argument that it is correct: the bound is what the language permits, not what the batteries happen to exercise, and the 6-mailbox world above is expressible today."}]},{"id":"blk-40818","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66505","text":"The three options, re-costed"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40820","spans":[{"id":"spn-66506","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-40821","spans":[{"id":"spn-66507","text":"option"}]},{"id":"blk-40822","spans":[{"id":"spn-66508","text":"cost"}]}],"id":"blk-40819","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40823","spans":[{"id":"spn-66509","marks":["bold"],"text":"(a)"}]},{"id":"blk-40824","spans":[{"id":"spn-66510","marks":["bold"],"text":"Golden-layer-only closure."},{"id":"spn-66511","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66512","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66513","text":" is Grounded in the language; the native reducer is a second opinion for route-free worlds only, stated as a documented boundary."}]},{"id":"blk-40825","spans":[{"id":"spn-66514","text":"Zero code. Slice B ships a permanently smaller proof surface than L-0, and \"two independent reducers agree\" stops being universally true."}]}],[{"id":"blk-40826","spans":[{"id":"spn-66515","marks":["bold"],"text":"(b)"}]},{"id":"blk-40827","spans":[{"id":"spn-66516","marks":["bold"],"text":"Steal a bit from `WIDX`."}]},{"id":"blk-40828","spans":[{"id":"spn-66517","marks":["bold"],"text":"Now measured as a conflict with your own route budget"},{"id":"spn-66518","text":" — needs mailboxes capped at 3. Not free; it spends a language bound."}]}],[{"id":"blk-40829","spans":[{"id":"spn-66519","marks":["bold"],"text":"(c)"}]},{"id":"blk-40830","spans":[{"id":"spn-66520","marks":["bold"],"text":"`FKEY_W` 52→53."},{"id":"spn-66521","text":" It is a "},{"id":"spn-66522","marks":["italic"],"text":"lowering-representation"},{"id":"spn-66523","text":" width strictly below the film: widening it moves no "},{"id":"spn-66524","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-66525","text":", no "},{"id":"spn-66526","marks":["code"],"text":"bknd-"},{"id":"spn-66527","text":", no film byte — only the reduced proof term."}]},{"id":"blk-40831","spans":[{"id":"spn-66528","text":"Needs your ruling on what the prohibition was protecting. If it protected the "},{"id":"spn-66529","marks":["bold"],"text":"semantic budget"},{"id":"spn-66530","text":", (c) is clean. If it protected the "},{"id":"spn-66531","marks":["bold"],"text":"ic32 term size"},{"id":"spn-66532","text":", (c) is out."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66533","marks":["bold"],"text":"My reading, offered as a recommendation and not a decision:"},{"id":"spn-66534","text":" (c) is now the cheapest honest option, because (b) turned out to spend a "},{"id":"spn-66535","marks":["italic"],"text":"language-visible"},{"id":"spn-66536","text":" bound to protect a "},{"id":"spn-66537","marks":["italic"],"text":"representation"},{"id":"spn-66538","text":" width — the more valuable of the two. But (c) rests entirely on what the "},{"id":"spn-66539","marks":["code"],"text":"FKEY_W"},{"id":"spn-66540","text":" prohibition was defending, which is yours to say, not mine to infer."}]},{"id":"blk-40833","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66541","text":"3. Autonomous decisions — please confirm or overrule"}]},{"id":"blk-40834","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66542","text":"(a) Two new laws, both refusals, both keyed by "},{"id":"spn-66543","marks":["bold"],"text":"epoch"}]},{"id":"blk-40835","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66544","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_BATCH"},{"id":"spn-66545","text":" is 4: one epoch's observation batch holds four claims. Six routes are legal ("},{"id":"spn-66546","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_ASYNC_ROUTES"},{"id":"spn-66547","text":" = "},{"id":"spn-66548","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-66549","text":" = 6) — but six routes "},{"id":"spn-66550","marks":["bold"],"text":"that all fire in the same epoch"},{"id":"spn-66551","text":" are not, because they would be handed to "},{"id":"spn-66552","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-66553","text":" as one batch of six and trip its assertion. Nothing checked this."}]},{"id":"blk-40836","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66554","marks":["bold"],"text":"`WRL_ROUTE_BATCH_OVERFLOW`"},{"id":"spn-66555","text":" — seal-time. Five routes co-firing on one"}]}],"id":"blk-40837","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66556","marks":["code"],"text":"once(1)"},{"id":"spn-66557","text":" Pulser is refused when the world is sealed."}]},{"id":"blk-40840","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66558","marks":["bold"],"text":"`WRL_EPOCH_BATCH_OVERFLOW`"},{"id":"spn-66559","text":" — fold-time. A world with 4 routes at epoch 1"}]}],"id":"blk-40841","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66560","text":"and a scenario that authors 1 claim at epoch 1 are "},{"id":"spn-66561","marks":["bold"],"text":"each"},{"id":"spn-66562","text":" legal and their "},{"id":"spn-66563","marks":["bold"],"text":"pairing"},{"id":"spn-66564","text":" is not."}]},{"id":"blk-40844","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66565","text":"They are deliberately "},{"id":"spn-66566","marks":["bold"],"text":"distinct codes from `WRL_ROUTE_BUDGET`"},{"id":"spn-66567","text":" and from each other, because the repairs are opposite: \"declare fewer routes\", \"declare them on different epochs\", \"edit the other file\". One code cannot ask for three things. R9g and mutation "},{"id":"spn-66568","marks":["bold"],"text":"M15"},{"id":"spn-66569","text":" hold that split; R10c holds that the pairing message names "},{"id":"spn-66570","marks":["italic"],"text":"which half"},{"id":"spn-66571","text":" is large, so the author knows which file to open."}]},{"id":"blk-40845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66572","text":"The pairing check is composed into the one "},{"id":"spn-66573","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"},{"id":"spn-66574","text":" door (the commit-3 argument, unchanged), "},{"id":"spn-66575","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-66576","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66577","marks":["code"],"text":"fold_batches"},{"id":"spn-66578","text":" re-checks on its own (R10g) — because a caller that never opens the door still must not be able to hand "},{"id":"spn-66579","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-66580","text":" a batch it will assert on. Mutation "},{"id":"spn-66581","marks":["bold"],"text":"M20"},{"id":"spn-66582","text":" is what proved the second check was reachable by nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-40846","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66583","text":"(b) The "},{"id":"spn-66584","marks":["code"],"text":"ir_to_fixture"},{"id":"spn-66585","text":" route refusal is "},{"id":"spn-66586","marks":["bold"],"text":"lifted"}]},{"id":"blk-40847","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66587","text":"Commits 2/3 refused a route-bearing artifact there, because a Fixture built from one silently dropped the routes and became an oracle for a "},{"id":"spn-66588","marks":["italic"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-66589","text":" world. Commit 4 makes the dropping "},{"id":"spn-66590","marks":["bold"],"text":"correct"},{"id":"spn-66591","text":" rather than silent: a route's runtime image is a claim, not structure — no port, no state, no edge, nothing the Fixture models. The Fixture of a route-bearing world "},{"id":"spn-66592","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-66593","text":" the Fixture of its route-free twin."}]},{"id":"blk-40848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66594","text":"That is a claim about structure, so it is measured as one. "},{"id":"spn-66595","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47"},{"id":"spn-66596","text":" P8d pushes five route-bearing variants' Fixtures through "},{"id":"spn-66597","marks":["code"],"text":"fixture_to_compile_plan_v1"},{"id":"spn-66598","text":" at a "},{"id":"spn-66599","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed"},{"id":"spn-66600","text":" semantic id — stripping the one field that could carry the difference for free — and all five collapse to "},{"id":"spn-66601","marks":["bold"],"text":"one plan digest"},{"id":"spn-66602","text":", while P8e shows the same five worlds keep five "},{"id":"spn-66603","marks":["bold"],"text":"distinct"},{"id":"spn-66604","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66605","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-"},{"id":"spn-66606","text":" ids. A collapse measured, not a comparison of one world with itself."}]},{"id":"blk-40849","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66607","text":"(c) The commit-3 carried obligation is "},{"id":"spn-66608","marks":["bold"],"text":"DECLINED"},{"id":"spn-66609","text":", with reasons"}]},{"id":"blk-40850","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66610","text":"Commit 3's memo promised to unify "},{"id":"spn-66611","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_canonical.route_body_in_range"},{"id":"spn-66612","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-66613","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-66614","text":" and remove the fork. "},{"id":"spn-66615","marks":["bold"],"text":"Working it through showed the unification is not free, and I did not do it."},{"id":"spn-66616","text":" The full argument is written into the function's docstring so it is not re-discovered; in short:"}]},{"id":"blk-40851","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66617","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-66618","text":" importing the spine would make the "},{"id":"spn-66619","marks":["bold"],"text":"frozen L-0 reducer"},{"id":"spn-66620","text":" depend on"}]}],"id":"blk-40852","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66621","text":"the module Slice B edits every commit — a language-track mistake would take the ratified tier red, the precise failure the sweep's frozen/live split exists to prevent;"}]},{"id":"blk-40855","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40857","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66622","text":"the spine importing "},{"id":"spn-66623","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-66624","text":" is the inversion the spine's header refuses, and"}]}],"id":"blk-40856","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40858","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66625","text":"refuses load-bearingly: the spine has a "},{"id":"spn-66626","marks":["bold"],"text":"verified browser port"},{"id":"spn-66627","text":", and a spine that reaches for the reducer cannot be ported;"}]},{"id":"blk-40859","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40861","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66628","text":"a third shared module ends the fork but adds a file to "},{"id":"spn-66629","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-66630","text":" dependency"}]}],"id":"blk-40860","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66631","text":"graphs, including the ported one."}]},{"id":"blk-40863","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66632","text":"So the fork stays, under the discipline every other derived constant is under: "},{"id":"spn-66633","marks":["bold"],"text":"an unavoidable second spelling is acceptable only when something fails the moment the two disagree."},{"id":"spn-66634","text":" That is "},{"id":"spn-66635","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47"},{"id":"spn-66636","text":" P0c, which folds the same bodies through both spellings across the whole boundary neighbourhood."}]},{"id":"blk-40864","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66637","text":"This is a judgement about which coupling is worse, not a fact, and it is reversible either way. Overrule freely."}]},{"id":"blk-40865","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66638","text":"(d) NEW — the declared-policy seam (a defect this commit found)"}]},{"id":"blk-40866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66639","text":"Not in the ruling. Found while rendering commit 4's first film, and it is the same defect as the route itself one layer down. A sealed world "},{"id":"spn-66640","marks":["bold"],"text":"carries"},{"id":"spn-66641","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-40867","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"semantic_policies = {..., \"admit_policy_id\": \"admit_mailbox_deliver_all_v1\",\n                          \"film_schema_id\":  \"film.v0.7.mailbox.v1\"}"},{"id":"blk-40868","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66642","text":"and "},{"id":"spn-66643","marks":["bold"],"text":"nothing in the tree read them."},{"id":"spn-66644","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66645","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-66646","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-66647","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"},{"id":"spn-66648","text":" defaults to the mailbox-*free* "},{"id":"spn-66649","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1"},{"id":"spn-66650","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-66651","marks":["code"],"text":"film_bytes_v7"},{"id":"spn-66652","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-66653","marks":["code"],"text":"mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-66654","text":" argument defaults to "},{"id":"spn-66655","marks":["code"],"text":"None"},{"id":"spn-66656","text":". Every fold harness in the tree was running a mailbox-bearing world under a reducer that does not know what a mailbox is, and rendering it with a projection that cannot show one."}]},{"id":"blk-40869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66657","text":"Measured on the first route-bearing world:"}]},{"id":"blk-40870","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"under the DEFAULT policy    claim ... payload=Send:#?:0.0.0.7\n                            (no admit_mailbox line, no mailbox line, no ledger)\nunder the DECLARED policy   claim ... payload=Send:mb:0.0.0.7\n                            ledger:MailboxEnqueue,mailbox=mb,epoch=1\n                            ledger:MailboxDeliver,mailbox=mb,epoch=2"},{"id":"blk-40871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66658","text":"The default reading loses the route's "},{"id":"spn-66659","marks":["bold"],"text":"entire effect"},{"id":"spn-66660","text":" and, worse, renders the target as "},{"id":"spn-66661","marks":["code"],"text":"#?"},{"id":"spn-66662","text":" — Film v0.7's "},{"id":"spn-66663","marks":["code"],"text":"INVALID_TARGET"},{"id":"spn-66664","text":". A film asserting the route addressed a mailbox that does not exist."}]},{"id":"blk-40872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66665","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime_seams(artifact, fx)"},{"id":"spn-66666","text":" returns "},{"id":"spn-66667","marks":["code"],"text":"(admit_policy_id, film_mailboxes)"},{"id":"spn-66668","text":" "},{"id":"spn-66669","marks":["bold"],"text":"together"},{"id":"spn-66670","text":", specifically so a caller cannot honour one and forget the other — mutations "},{"id":"spn-66671","marks":["bold"],"text":"M11"},{"id":"spn-66672","text":" (mailboxes forgotten) and "},{"id":"spn-66673","marks":["bold"],"text":"M12"},{"id":"spn-66674","text":" (policy forgotten) are the two halves, and both are caught. R7g/R7h are the sharpest rows: two routes to "},{"id":"spn-66675","marks":["bold"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-66676","text":" mailbox, because the two policies differ only in how they accumulate several claims on one key — under the declared policy both messages are delivered, under the old default "},{"id":"spn-66677","marks":["bold"],"text":"one is silently dropped"},{"id":"spn-66678","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40873","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66679","marks":["code"],"text":"film_mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-66680","text":" returning "},{"id":"spn-66681","marks":["code"],"text":"[]"},{"id":"spn-66682","text":" for a mailbox-free world is deliberate and load-bearing: Film v0.7 gates its whole mailbox block on "},{"id":"spn-66683","marks":["code"],"text":"if mailboxes:"},{"id":"spn-66684","text":", so every pre-Slice-B world folds "},{"id":"spn-66685","marks":["bold"],"text":"byte-identically"},{"id":"spn-66686","text":" under the declared seams and under the old defaults (R11b)."}]},{"id":"blk-40874","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66687","text":"(e) ScenarioV1 "},{"id":"spn-66688","marks":["bold"],"text":"cannot express"},{"id":"spn-66689","text":" a "},{"id":"spn-66690","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"}]},{"id":"blk-40875","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66691","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario._OPERATIONS"},{"id":"spn-66692","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-66693","marks":["code"],"text":"(\"SetRotor\", \"ResetFault\")"},{"id":"spn-66694","text":". So the Q4 writer-15 reservation is guarding a door that is "},{"id":"spn-66695","marks":["bold"],"text":"already shut for a second, independent reason"},{"id":"spn-66696","text":". Recorded rather than acted on: the twin proof (R5) therefore builds its hand-written claim with "},{"id":"spn-66697","marks":["code"],"text":"mk_claim"},{"id":"spn-66698","text":" rather than as a ScenarioV1 claim. If you want authored "},{"id":"spn-66699","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"},{"id":"spn-66700","text":" claims in scenarios, that is a ruling, not an oversight to fix quietly."}]},{"id":"blk-40876","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66701","text":"(f) "},{"id":"spn-66702","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run3o"},{"id":"spn-66703","text":" parameterised rather than forked — "},{"id":"spn-66704","marks":["bold"],"text":"and it was hiding a defect"}]},{"id":"blk-40877","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66705","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47._fold"},{"id":"spn-66706","text":" always took an "},{"id":"spn-66707","marks":["code"],"text":"fx"},{"id":"spn-66708","text":" argument, but "},{"id":"spn-66709","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run3o"},{"id":"spn-66710","text":"'s golden half closed over that battery's module global "},{"id":"spn-66711","marks":["code"],"text":"FX = mkfx(8, 4)"},{"id":"spn-66712","text":" and the argument reached only the IC half. **The row passed because the demo world "},{"id":"spn-66713","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-66714","text":" structurally "},{"id":"spn-66715","marks":["code"],"text":"mkfx(8, 4)"},{"id":"spn-66716","text":"** — the two halves were comparing the same world by accident, not by construction, and would have started comparing two "},{"id":"spn-66717","marks":["italic"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-66718","text":" worlds, silently and greenly, the first time commit 4 folded a mailbox-bearing one."}]},{"id":"blk-40878","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66719","text":"Fixed with a defaulted "},{"id":"spn-66720","marks":["code"],"text":"fx=None"},{"id":"spn-66721","text":" on eight helpers, "},{"id":"spn-66722","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-66723","text":" a second copy of the driver in the new battery. Every existing call site is byte-identical and the frozen rows re-run unchanged (5/5 PASS, 42s)."}]},{"id":"blk-40879","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66724","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run3o"},{"id":"spn-66725","text":" is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-66726","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-66727","text":" added to "},{"id":"spn-66728","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep"},{"id":"spn-66729","text":" — it is an ADMIT battery, not a WRL one, and widening what that sweep covers would change what its number means. It was re-run by hand; the reasoning is a comment in the sweep."}]},{"id":"blk-40880","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66730","text":"4. What the mutation round found"}]},{"id":"blk-40881","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66731","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate49"},{"id":"spn-66732","text":" runs 22 mutations including a null control and two "},{"id":"spn-66733","marks":["code"],"text":"@noop"},{"id":"spn-66734","text":" rewrites that "},{"id":"spn-66735","marks":["bold"],"text":"must survive"},{"id":"spn-66736","text":" (a harness that \"catches\" a no-op proves nothing)."}]},{"id":"blk-40882","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66737","marks":["bold"],"text":"M7 — the claim numbered by STORAGE order instead of canonical order. SURVIVED the first spelling, with nothing red."},{"id":"spn-66738","text":" The most useful finding, and it is the same finding as M8 one layer up. R1c is the row that compares "},{"id":"spn-66739","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-66740","text":" against the canonical accessor rather than a literal, so it is the row one would expect to catch this — and it "},{"id":"spn-66741","marks":["bold"],"text":"cannot"},{"id":"spn-66742","text":", because canonicalization sorts "},{"id":"spn-66743","marks":["code"],"text":"async_routes"},{"id":"spn-66744","text":" into RouteKey order "},{"id":"spn-66745","marks":["bold"],"text":"before sealing"},{"id":"spn-66746","text":". On any artifact "},{"id":"spn-66747","marks":["code"],"text":"lower()"},{"id":"spn-66748","text":" produces, "},{"id":"spn-66749","marks":["code"],"text":"enumerate(routes)"},{"id":"spn-66750","text":" and the canonical ordinal are the same function; authoring order cannot separate them because the seal has already erased it. "},{"id":"spn-66751","marks":["bold"],"text":"R1e exists because of this line"},{"id":"spn-66752","text":": it hands the fold a deliberately un-canonically-ordered route list — the one input on which \"numbered by key\" and \"numbered by position\" disagree — and R1f then shows the fold's "},{"id":"spn-66753","marks":["italic"],"text":"output"},{"id":"spn-66754","text":" does not inherit that disorder. M7's expected-catch list names only R1e; listing R1c as well would have been the comfortable lie, leaving the mutant reported as survived while blaming a row that physically cannot catch it."}]},{"id":"blk-40883","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66755","marks":["bold"],"text":"M8 — the canonical sort dropped. SURVIVED the first spelling."},{"id":"spn-66756","text":" Same root: for every single-epoch world the sort is a no-op. It is load-bearing only where canonical order and "},{"id":"spn-66757","marks":["bold"],"text":"epoch"},{"id":"spn-66758","text":" order disagree — a world whose first-sorting route fires last. "},{"id":"spn-66759","marks":["bold"],"text":"R3b is that world."}]},{"id":"blk-40884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66760","marks":["bold"],"text":"M10 — `fold_script` grows its own injection."},{"id":"spn-66761","text":" Caught only after R4 was rewritten to use three co-firing routes: with "},{"id":"spn-66762","marks":["bold"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-66763","text":" route a truncating second injection agreed by coincidence."}]},{"id":"blk-40885","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66764","marks":["bold"],"text":"M12 — the policy half forgotten."},{"id":"spn-66765","text":" Caught only after R7g/R7h were added, for the reason in §3d: the two policies are indistinguishable on a world with one message."}]},{"id":"blk-40886","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66766","marks":["bold"],"text":"M20 — `_assert_capacity` deleted from the merge."},{"id":"spn-66767","text":" Reached by no row until R10g/R10h were added. A law nothing exercises is a comment."}]},{"id":"blk-40887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66768","text":"Four rows in this battery (R1e, R1f, R3b, R7g/R7h, R10g/R10h) exist "},{"id":"spn-66769","marks":["bold"],"text":"only"},{"id":"spn-66770","text":" because a mutation walked through the first spelling. That is the round working."}]},{"id":"blk-40888","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66771","text":"5. Not frozen"}]},{"id":"blk-40889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66772","text":"Commit 4 is the last commit in the ruled Slice B line, so the ruling's own next step is: "},{"id":"spn-66773","marks":["bold"],"text":"freeze the Slice B line, then promote `~~` to Grounded in `WRL_CORE_0.1.md` §14."}]},{"id":"blk-40890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66774","text":"I have not done either, because "},{"id":"spn-66775","marks":["bold"],"text":"§2 blocks it."},{"id":"spn-66776","text":" Promoting "},{"id":"spn-66777","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-66778","text":" to Grounded while the native reducer cannot fold one would publish a tier claim the tree cannot honour. The three options in §2 are the fork in the road; (a) also requires deciding what \"Grounded\" means when one of the two reducers is out of scope for the construct."}]},{"id":"blk-40891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66779","text":"Everything else is ready. Say the word and the freeze is mechanical."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera37wkywzvxndhpwkwzszjgin7tyfdyu5xtepiv65tivpr2o3p74ea","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}